  TOY-NULL RESULT: the E=4·V=8·d=6 600-step SKEWED regime DOES NOT
    reproduce the M4b production collapse. Baseline cell-A already
    achieves 4/4 distinct_experts + identity decode → there is no
    collapse to escape. All 4 cells land on byte-identical decode
    (LZ_norm = 0.0360459) because CE convergence dominates
    the aux perturbation at this scale.
  MECHANISTIC CHECK (aux gradient injection works as designed):
    cell-a  none  H(gate) = 0.145866 (uniform = 1.38629)
    cell-b  ent   H(gate) = 1.15225 ← H_686 pushed +1.00638 toward uniform ✓
    cell-c  kl    H(gate) = 0.169797 (KL acts on output, not router)
    cell-d  both  H(gate) = 1.18533 ← combined ent+kl ✓
    → H_686 aux gradient does move the router toward uniform but
      this regime is below the collapse threshold so no decode
      diversity gain is observable. H_687 leaves router-H near
      baseline (acts on output distribution) — as expected.
  VERDICT: H_686/H_687 toy ablation INDETERMINATE — neither
    confirms nor refutes production escape. The production fire
    (V=151643, real M4b regime) is the only valid test.
